WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.570
What?! Eichi is at Narita Airport?

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:06.230
Just before the Fantasia
Music Festival's rehearsal,

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:08.870
Mitsuki receives another
fake email from Izumi.

00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:12.230
Mitsuki is waiting at the airport,
and Takuto decides to tell her the truth.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:15.570
But Mitsuki isn't discouraged
by the news,

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:17.730
and she goes on to win
the Best New Singer Award!

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.370
You did great, Mitsuki!

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:23.100
So, I wonder what's going to
happen today...

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:28.730
Got that?

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:29.800
Yes.

00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:14.230
Good morning.

00:02:14.470 --> 00:02:15.470
Morning!

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:17.970
Congratulations on
the Best New Singer Award!

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:19.470
Thank you very much!

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:25.730
Thanks to the award, I get to go to America.
I'm so happy I can't stand it!

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:29.700
How nice! Share a little bit
of your happiness with me!

00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:32.370
Well, Ms. Oda, why don't you come
to the Christmas party?

00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:36.030
We're talking about doing it at
Ms. Oshige's house on Christmas Eve.

00:02:37.130 --> 00:02:40.470
A Christmas party? It kind of sounds like
an elementary school kid's way of saying it.

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:42.470
What? Yeah, maybe.

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:46.500
<i>But I have work</i>
<i>on Christmas Eve.</i>

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:48.370
<i>Aww, that's too bad!</i>

00:02:48.830 --> 00:02:50.830
Seems like she's super excited.

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:53.670
She's so close to finding out
where Eichi is.

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:55.900
She's so happy she
can't contain herself.

00:02:56.330 --> 00:02:57.730
<i>Well, shall we start</i>
<i>recording soon?</i>

00:02:57.930 --> 00:02:58.600
Sure!

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:02.300
Okay, this program is going to
be aired on Christmas Eve,

00:03:02.330 --> 00:03:04.830
so let's do this
like it's the 24th.

00:03:04.930 --> 00:03:05.600
Okay!

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:12.830
Hello, everyone! Merry Christmas!
Well, our guest tonight is...

00:03:12.970 --> 00:03:15.100
Full Moon! Merry Christmas!

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.530
Ms. Oshige and me...

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:29.030
Wakana, Tomoe...

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:32.230
There they are!

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:33.330
Good morning!

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:34.570
Oh, morning!

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:35.270
Morning.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:38.470
Hey Kumi, Emi, do you have
plans on Christmas Eve?

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:39.970
No, why?

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:42.300
I'm going to have a Christmas party
with everybody.

00:03:42.330 --> 00:03:43.570
- A Christmas party?!
- A Christmas party?!

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:45.700
Yeah! Do you two
wanna come?

00:03:46.130 --> 00:03:49.430
We'll decorate the door with a wreath,
exchange presents and stuff.

00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:51.430
It'll definitely be fun!

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:53.230
Yeah, sounds good.

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:56.200
And it's our last Christmas as
elementary school students!

00:03:56.370 --> 00:03:58.130
Yep! Let's all have fun together.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:08.930
So look here, you do this...

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:11.100
Then this, then this...

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:12.670
You put a ribbon on it...

00:04:13.070 --> 00:04:14.400
And the wreath is complete!

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:17.900
- The Forest Friends Play!
- The Forest Friends Play!

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:24.570
At Christmas, hanging a wreath on the door
or a wall is supposed to attract happiness.

00:04:25.170 --> 00:04:26.630
Everyone in front of the TV,

00:04:26.670 --> 00:04:30.000
hang a wreath on the door
for Christmas, and let's be happy!

00:04:30.170 --> 00:04:34.500
We Death Spirits don't really have
anything to do with Christmas though.

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:39.400
No way! Death Spirits want to be
happy on Christmas too!

00:04:39.730 --> 00:04:41.100
Mitsuki, you're so good.

00:04:41.430 --> 00:04:44.870
Before I moved in with my grandma,
I made them every year.

00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:47.000
Oh, you mean...

00:04:47.230 --> 00:04:50.370
They bring back special memories
you made with Eichi?!

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:51.070
What?!

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:58.630
<i>It's a beautiful wreath, Mitsuki.</i>

00:05:00.130 --> 00:05:02.530
<i>If the wreath is made</i>
<i>by you, Mitsuki,</i>

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:04.800
<i>I feel like it's really going to</i>
<i>bring me happiness.</i>

00:05:07.230 --> 00:05:11.570
<i>I hope that Eichi and me,</i>
<i>and everyone will find happiness.</i>

00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:19.430
You're so lucky, Mitsuki!

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:20.300
What?

00:05:20.330 --> 00:05:22.100
Oh, I'm jealous!

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:23.130
Yeah, yeah.

00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:28.170
Hey, I know, how about if we invite boys
for Christmas? Okay, Kumi?

00:05:28.230 --> 00:05:28.900
What?!

00:05:34.870 --> 00:05:36.100
It'll be your chance!

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:38.500
Then, is that okay?

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:40.070
- Yeah!
- Yeah!

00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:44.500
Kumi, Wakana...

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:46.570
Emi, and then...

00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:49.100
Yeah, yeah, it doesn't matter
how many people,

00:05:49.130 --> 00:05:51.170
so invite everyone
and we'll party!

00:05:51.570 --> 00:05:52.630
Okay.

00:05:52.930 --> 00:05:55.330
But I wonder if it's okay
to invite classmates.

00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:58.800
That's right, how will you
explain Ms. Oshige.

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:03.630
That's no problem.
You can tell them that I'm like a big sister.

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:06.170
"Big sister," really?

00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:07.930
I don't think you'd pass.

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:10.000
What are you two saying!

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:13.370
That's why I said "like"
a big sister. Jeez!

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:21.370
My CD is finally done.

00:06:21.930 --> 00:06:26.530
Mr. Takasu wanted to release
your CD within the year,

00:06:26.570 --> 00:06:28.470
and he did everything possible
to make it happen.

00:06:29.270 --> 00:06:32.930
The release date is towards
the very end of the year...December 24th.

00:06:33.570 --> 00:06:35.100
December 24th?

00:06:36.570 --> 00:06:39.900
Don't get spoiled by
your Christmas present.

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:44.700
It's a humble celebration for
the new Madoka Wakamatsu

00:06:44.730 --> 00:06:47.530
who could finally get
her start as a singer.

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:50.900
Thank you so much.

00:06:53.330 --> 00:06:55.770
I see. A Christmas party, huh?

00:06:56.270 --> 00:06:58.500
Dr. Wakaoji, you should come too.

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:01.070
Sorry, I have to work that day.

00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:02.270
What?!

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:05.730
But if I can go home early,
I'll swing by.

00:07:06.770 --> 00:07:07.430
Okay!

00:07:10.370 --> 00:07:12.070
<i>So, you saw it, right?</i>

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:15.470
<i>Yes, the husband came</i>
<i>down from the second floor</i>

00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:17.400
<i>and said that</i>
<i>he wanted coffee.</i>

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:19.830
<i>So I thought I'd make it, but the wife said</i>
<i>she would make it, which she rarely does.</i>

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:20.870
Ms. Tanaka...

00:07:20.900 --> 00:07:21.900
Yes?

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:27.000
Wow! Fuyuko Komaki's
Christmas Dinner Show?!

00:07:27.530 --> 00:07:30.000
It's a little early,
but it's a Christmas present.

00:07:30.430 --> 00:07:35.600
Th-Thank you very much!
I can't believe you were able to get a ticket.

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:39.530
I got it from Ms. Oshige.
But I can't go.

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:40.870
Oh, I see.

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:45.400
But it's such a nice thing!
It's too much! Oh, I know!

00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:51.800
Here, this is a gift in return.

00:07:51.830 --> 00:07:52.900
A radio?

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:55.700
I won it in a lottery when
I was out shopping.

00:07:55.800 --> 00:07:58.070
I already have a radio.

00:08:02.230 --> 00:08:04.300
This will be a secret from
your grandmother!

00:08:06.870 --> 00:08:09.230
I am so happy,
I am so happy!

00:08:09.400 --> 00:08:13.470
Oh, yes! I have to listen to all of
Fuyuko Komaki's CDs again.

00:08:15.130 --> 00:08:17.270
<i>Well then, the fax theme</i>
<i>for this evening is,</i>

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:20.830
<i>"Christmas is almost here!</i>
<i>What do you want for a present?!"</i>

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:24.170
I'm giving my grandma a knit shawl.

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:29.200
A hand knit present, huh?
You put so much into it, Mitsuki.

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:33.470
Think of your body...
and don't overdo it.

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:40.430
Hey, are there Christmas presents
in the world of Death Spirits?

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:42.600
It's not that there aren't, but...

00:08:42.970 --> 00:08:46.470
Well, why don't you knit
a present for Takuto too?

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:51.370
Oh, are you not good at knitting?

00:08:51.930 --> 00:08:54.070
No, but...is it okay?

00:08:54.270 --> 00:08:54.930
What?

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:59.400
No... Umm... You're right!
It's Christmas!

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:01.700
Yes, let's all be happy!

00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:04.930
I want to be happy too.

00:09:06.700 --> 00:09:09.600
On Christmas Eve, I'm going to give Takuto
a present and confess my love!

00:09:10.100 --> 00:09:10.770
Yeah!

00:09:11.170 --> 00:09:12.770
<i>And now one song.</i>

00:09:16.670 --> 00:09:19.930
<i>This song will be released</i>
<i>on December 24th,</i>

00:09:19.970 --> 00:09:22.400
<i>and it is Madoka Wakamatsu's</i>
<i>debut single.</i>

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:24.400
<i>It's a cover of</i>
<i>a Route L song,</i>

00:09:24.430 --> 00:09:27.130
<i>and it was a hot topic when</i>
<i>she competed with Full Moon.</i>

00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:30.370
<i>It's a little bit late,</i>
<i>but it's finally on sale.</i>

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:33.400
<i>Her version is more rhythmic.</i>

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:36.900
<i>If you give this to the person you like</i>
<i>for Christmas, I'm sure things will go well!</i>

00:09:37.070 --> 00:09:39.430
<i>Here is Madoka Wakamtsu's,</i>
<i>"Eternal Snow"!</i>

00:09:40.630 --> 00:09:47.370
<i>How long has it been</i>
<i>since I fell in love with you?</i>

00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:54.430
<i>- My feelings keep getting stronger...</i>
- Madoka... That's great.

00:09:54.930 --> 00:10:01.800
<i>I wonder if you can notice them.</i>

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:09.170
<i>Even though I've</i>
<i>never mentioned it.</i>

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:16.100
<i>They're silent like the snow,</i>

00:10:16.570 --> 00:10:24.000
<i>but they keep building up.</i>

00:10:24.030 --> 00:10:26.500
<i>Hold me tight,</i>

00:10:26.600 --> 00:10:35.570
<i>if loving someone</i>
<i>was going to feel like this</i>

00:10:35.670 --> 00:10:38.570
<i>I wish I never found out</i>
<i>about love.</i>

00:10:38.800 --> 00:10:40.600
<i>I love you.</i>

00:10:40.800 --> 00:10:44.770
<i>My tears won't stop.</i>

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:46.870
<i>If this is how it's going to be...</i>

00:10:46.900 --> 00:10:56.100
<i>It would have been better...</i>
<i>I wish I had never met you!</i>

00:10:57.270 --> 00:10:58.270
Hey, Meroko.

00:10:58.600 --> 00:10:59.270
Hmm?

00:10:59.500 --> 00:11:03.770
Let's keep this a secret from Takuto until
Christmas Eve and surprise him, okay?

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:05.270
Yeah!

00:11:19.230 --> 00:11:23.270
<i>I'm sure that Christmas</i>
<i>this year is going to be lovely.</i>

00:11:41.530 --> 00:11:43.070
Okay, I'll see you on the 24th!

00:11:43.270 --> 00:11:45.770
At four o'clock in front of
the shopping mall, right?

00:11:46.030 --> 00:11:46.700
Yeah!

00:11:46.730 --> 00:11:49.630
Mitsuki, Kumi invited Machida too!

00:11:49.770 --> 00:11:50.430
Really?!

00:11:51.800 --> 00:11:52.470
Yeah.

00:11:52.900 --> 00:11:54.770
Wow! That's great!

00:11:55.630 --> 00:11:56.830
Okay, bye!

00:11:57.100 --> 00:11:58.100
- Bye!
- Bye!

00:11:59.700 --> 00:12:03.200
What's up with that Meroko lately?

00:12:03.370 --> 00:12:04.370
What do you mean?

00:12:04.470 --> 00:12:07.370
Both yesterday and today,
she said, "I'm sleepy"

00:12:07.400 --> 00:12:09.170
and wouldn't even come with you.

00:12:09.670 --> 00:12:12.270
I'm sure that she's doing something
in the middle of the night.

00:12:13.330 --> 00:12:15.200
Girls have a lot of things to do.

00:12:15.300 --> 00:12:16.300
Like what?

00:12:16.470 --> 00:12:18.270
Just a lot of things...

00:12:24.070 --> 00:12:28.730
Yep, I'm sure that Grandma will
be happy to receive this.

00:12:29.370 --> 00:12:30.900
Oh, you're so lucky, Mitsuki.

00:12:31.770 --> 00:12:33.730
I haven't even scratched
the surface of my scarf.

00:12:36.570 --> 00:12:38.430
Well, if it's come to this,
I'll use my powers!

00:12:40.670 --> 00:12:43.700
If you don't knit it all
with your own hands,

00:12:43.730 --> 00:12:45.830
you won't be able to convey
your feelings to Takuto.

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:50.870
What are you talking about
in the middle of the night?

00:12:50.900 --> 00:12:52.570
Whoa! Nothing!

00:12:52.770 --> 00:12:53.430
Th-That's right.

00:12:53.570 --> 00:12:54.570
It's nothing.

00:12:55.200 --> 00:12:59.470
It's okay to be excited for Christmas,
but keep it in check.

00:12:59.730 --> 00:13:01.130
- Okay!
- Okay!

00:13:14.430 --> 00:13:15.430
Grandma?

00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:19.370
You could at least answer!

00:13:19.400 --> 00:13:20.070
Meroko!

00:13:20.630 --> 00:13:22.430
Umm... Grandma...

00:13:23.370 --> 00:13:28.200
I've made plans with my friends today.
I'll come home before it gets too late.

00:13:28.970 --> 00:13:30.070
May I go—

00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:31.700
Do as you like.

00:13:32.430 --> 00:13:34.600
Th-Thank you!

00:13:41.400 --> 00:13:42.930
Well, I'm off!

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:55.900
Oh, she's here!

00:13:56.070 --> 00:13:57.430
Mitsuki!

00:13:57.470 --> 00:13:58.470
Everyone!

00:13:59.070 --> 00:14:00.470
Wow...

00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:08.000
It's a beautiful tree, isn't it?

00:14:08.530 --> 00:14:11.100
I'm sure it's even more
beautiful in the evening.

00:14:11.170 --> 00:14:13.230
It's romantic.

00:14:14.130 --> 00:14:16.930
I've decided to confess to
Takuto over there!

00:14:17.170 --> 00:14:19.070
Oh, I think that will be lovely.

00:14:19.430 --> 00:14:21.130
What are you whispering about?

00:14:21.500 --> 00:14:23.130
Oh, nothing!

00:14:23.170 --> 00:14:24.870
It's a secret.

00:14:25.330 --> 00:14:26.000
Huh?

00:14:26.600 --> 00:14:27.800
What is it with those two?

00:14:56.400 --> 00:14:58.670
- Merry Christmas!
- Merry Christmas!

00:16:57.700 --> 00:16:59.730
Hey, what happened to everyone?

00:17:03.330 --> 00:17:05.030
Umm... Machida...

00:17:11.170 --> 00:17:11.830
Umm...

00:17:18.100 --> 00:17:19.830
- Please go out with me!
- Please go out with me!

00:17:21.230 --> 00:17:23.330
- Yay!
- Yay!

00:17:26.500 --> 00:17:28.200
Come to think of it, where is Meroko?

00:17:29.870 --> 00:17:33.030
Oh, Takuto.
You have something in your pocket.

00:17:33.130 --> 00:17:33.800
Huh?

00:17:37.670 --> 00:17:40.830
So I'm supposed to clean
this up by myself?

00:17:42.600 --> 00:17:43.600
Yes?

00:17:45.200 --> 00:17:47.900
Oh, Dr. Wakaoji...

00:17:48.130 --> 00:17:49.200
Merry Christmas.

00:17:49.700 --> 00:17:52.330
Huh? Is it all over?

00:17:52.900 --> 00:17:53.900
No, no.

00:17:54.100 --> 00:17:57.100
There's still some food left over,
so let's make a toast!

00:18:06.300 --> 00:18:08.770
I'LL BE WAITING AT
THE TOP OF THE TREE
IN THE SHOPPING MALL PLAZA.
—MEROKO

00:18:12.200 --> 00:18:13.200
Meroko.

00:18:14.530 --> 00:18:18.030
What is this?
You could've just told me this.

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:19.570
But...

00:18:26.570 --> 00:18:28.800
I wanted to give this to you
in front of this tree.

00:18:32.070 --> 00:18:35.570
You... Is this what you've been
sneaking around to do lately?

00:18:36.270 --> 00:18:42.770
It's Christmas! It's the first Christmas
since Green Onion Ramen was formed.

00:18:43.830 --> 00:18:46.500
Mitsuki taught me,
and I knit it the best that I could.

00:18:46.870 --> 00:18:47.600
What?

00:18:48.800 --> 00:18:49.470
<i>She taught you?</i>

00:18:52.370 --> 00:18:57.170
Takuto... I've been given the cold shoulder
many times, but I'll keep confessing.

00:18:58.500 --> 00:19:01.370
Takuto, I really like you.

00:19:02.800 --> 00:19:03.470
What?

00:19:04.800 --> 00:19:06.470
Oh, I understand.

00:19:06.900 --> 00:19:08.330
You just...

00:19:09.630 --> 00:19:11.330
I've confessed 58 times,

00:19:11.370 --> 00:19:13.630
and this is the first time you didn't let it
go in one ear and out the other.

00:19:13.870 --> 00:19:18.030
W-Well, it's the first Christmas
since we've met.

00:19:18.400 --> 00:19:19.070
So...

00:19:19.230 --> 00:19:23.670
D-Don't get the wrong idea.
I don't especially like anyone...

00:19:28.400 --> 00:19:32.730
I'm unsure of...my feelings.

00:19:34.900 --> 00:19:36.630
That's okay.

00:19:38.370 --> 00:19:43.430
Compared to the past,
this is major progress. I'm satisfied.

00:19:44.930 --> 00:19:45.930
This is great.

00:19:50.430 --> 00:19:51.500
H-Hey!

00:19:52.800 --> 00:19:54.730
Wrap this around yourself too.

00:19:55.570 --> 00:19:57.470
Aww, Takuto!

00:19:57.500 --> 00:19:58.770
I know, I know.

00:19:59.200 --> 00:20:00.570
Stop crying.

00:20:07.270 --> 00:20:08.470
Yay!

00:20:08.800 --> 00:20:12.370
- Yahoo! Jingle, jingle...
- Hmm, 58 times, huh?

00:20:12.400 --> 00:20:15.100
I let it go in one ear and
out the other 83 times.

00:20:15.300 --> 00:20:20.300
Who cares about that this evening?
Merry Christmas, everyone!

00:20:20.630 --> 00:20:22.900
Okay, smile, smile!

00:20:23.400 --> 00:20:26.530
Huh? I don't understand
how to work the flash!

00:20:28.930 --> 00:20:30.930
What are you doing? C'mon!

00:20:30.970 --> 00:20:33.270
Actually, I have a present for
the two of you as well.

00:20:34.170 --> 00:20:34.830
Here you go.

00:20:35.370 --> 00:20:36.800
It's cute!

00:20:37.000 --> 00:20:39.300
Mitsuki, you made these for us?

00:20:40.870 --> 00:20:41.870
Hey Takuto!

00:20:42.100 --> 00:20:42.770
Yeah!

00:20:43.100 --> 00:20:43.770
Okay!

00:20:47.870 --> 00:20:49.870
Green Onion Ramen returns the favor!

00:20:58.000 --> 00:20:59.000
It's snowing!

00:20:59.070 --> 00:21:00.370
Yeah!

00:21:00.430 --> 00:21:02.200
Wow, so pretty!

00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:10.300
<i>Hello, everyone! Merry Christmas!</i>
<i>Well, our guest tonight is...</i>

00:21:10.630 --> 00:21:13.270
<i>Full Moon!</i>
<i>Merry Christmas, everyone!</i>

00:21:13.300 --> 00:21:15.430
<i>- Thanks for joining us tonight.</i>
<i>- Thanks you for having me!</i>

00:21:15.570 --> 00:21:18.730
<i>Well, why don't we start with the song?</i>
<i>Will you introduce it for us?</i>

00:21:18.970 --> 00:21:19.630
<i>Sure!</i>

00:21:19.870 --> 00:21:23.730
<i>From the bottom of my heart,</i>
<i>I hope you all have a wonderful Christmas.</i>

00:21:24.170 --> 00:21:26.070
<i>This is Full Moon,</i>
<i>and here is my song, "Eternal Snow."</i>

00:23:06.600 --> 00:23:08.530
Oh no! This is bad!

00:23:08.630 --> 00:23:09.630
I know!

00:23:09.770 --> 00:23:11.070
We were so caught up in the excitement
over the Best New Singer Award

00:23:11.100 --> 00:23:13.030
that we forgot to think about
her grandmother!

00:23:13.300 --> 00:23:16.330
Isn't there some way to convince her
to let her go to America?

00:23:16.370 --> 00:23:17.600
There's no way!

00:23:17.700 --> 00:23:21.370
We have to keep it a secret that
it's the prize for winning the award!

00:23:21.700 --> 00:23:22.700
Oh, more bad news!

00:23:22.730 --> 00:23:24.730
She got in a fight with
her grandmother!

00:23:26.500 --> 00:23:30.070
Next time on Full Moon:
"Grandma's Past"

00:23:30.600 --> 00:23:31.600
- Look forward to it!
- Look forward to it!
